WEBVTT

00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:08.375
Very warm.

00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:11.958
[♪ hopeful music playing]

00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:15.416
[Gary sighs]

00:00:18.541 --> 00:00:21.208
Permission to hug?

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.416
[grunts]

00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:34.416
[exhales deeply]

00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:41.791
We're gonna save you
and save your friend.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:45.083
-[exhales]
-Judy! [screams]

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:46.750
Hey, he's gonna eat
that rabbit!

00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:48.708
No, wait! [stammers]
I'm saving her!

00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:50.125
I'm gonna get her
the anti-pen.

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:51.666
Where is she?

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.541
[sighs] She...
She didn't make it.

00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:55.708
[♪ tense music playing]

00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:59.208
But with snake bites,
you go fast.

00:01:00.666 --> 00:01:01.708
You'll see.

00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:05.375
[grunting]

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:07.125
[gasps, groans]

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.666
[grunting]

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.583
-[Gary panting]
-[Chèvre yells]

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:13.375
[gasps] No.

00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:15.208
[all grunting]

00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.500
[grunting]

00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:22.541
She's gone, Nick.
Just get it over with!

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:23.625
[Nick grunts]

00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:28.916
[all grunting]

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.208
[Gary gasps]

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.583
-[Higgins grunts]
-[Gary gasps]

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.208
[gasps]

00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:37.583
-[grunting]
-You're done.

00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:40.791
-Know when to quit!
-[grunts]

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:42.500
[Gary] Anti-venom!

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:45.750
You can save her with the
anti-venom! Throw me the bag!

00:01:45.833 --> 00:01:47.041
[Bloats grunts]

00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:48.333
Judy!

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.541
[Pawbert groans]

00:01:57.458 --> 00:01:58.625
[both straining]

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:04.583
[grunts]

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.875
Leave it!
You're gonna kill us both.

00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:10.458
It's not worth dying for.

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:14.125
Agree to disagree.

00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:18.416
[grunts]

00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:23.916
[Nick yelps]

00:02:25.708 --> 00:02:27.583
[anti-venom pen]
Stab me
straight into the heart.

00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:28.791
[gasps]

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.333
[groans]

00:02:43.875 --> 00:02:46.125
[screaming]

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.250
[Gary grunts]

00:02:48.041 --> 00:02:49.666
[both grunting]

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.208
[both panting]

00:02:54.083 --> 00:02:55.208
[exhales]

00:02:58.458 --> 00:03:00.666
-I thought... He told me you...
-I was trying to get to you.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.166
-And I saw you...
-...that you were...

00:03:04.916 --> 00:03:07.500
I'll help your friend.

00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:12.583
Okay. [stammers] I don't care
that we're different.

00:03:12.666 --> 00:03:14.333
You know? I...

00:03:14.416 --> 00:03:17.708
What I care about is you.

00:03:17.791 --> 00:03:19.458
I care about you.

00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:22.208
Okay?

00:03:23.958 --> 00:03:25.250
And I didn't say it.

00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:27.625
I should've said it.

00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:28.875
But I didn't

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.708
because...

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:33.791
uh, well... [chuckles]

00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:36.541
...'cause I am
an emotionally insecure

00:03:36.625 --> 00:03:39.291
source of your discomfort,

00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:42.166
who's not good
at expressing his feelings.

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:45.791
Probably because I've been
on my own my whole life.

00:03:45.875 --> 00:03:47.416
It's not an excuse.
It's just...

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.083
It's why instead
of telling you

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:53.250
that you're the best thing
that ever happened to me,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.291
I-I make jokes
about your ears.

00:03:56.375 --> 00:03:58.000
And-And I tell you
that you try too hard,

00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:59.833
when, you know, the truth is

00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:03.041
I just don't want you
to get hurt.

00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:05.333
Because... [breathes deeply]

00:04:05.416 --> 00:04:07.416
Because no one else
in the world

00:04:07.916 --> 00:04:10.750
matters more to me
than you do.

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:11.916
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:15.333
I... I do try too hard
because deep down

00:04:15.416 --> 00:04:17.083
I'm afraid that I am
what everyone thinks I am.

00:04:17.166 --> 00:04:18.791
And I suppress my discomfort
because I'm worried

00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:20.500
it makes me look weak,
and I wanna be strong,

00:04:20.583 --> 00:04:21.666
and I think I'm failing
all the time.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.166
And I only take
what you say personally

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.666
because you're
the only one in my life

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:25.958
who ever believed in me,

00:04:26.041 --> 00:04:27.833
even when I don't even
believe in myself.

00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:29.875
[inhales deeply] And I
should have told you that.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.125
No one else in the world
matters to me

00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:34.458
more than you do either.

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:37.958
I have unresolved
childhood trauma

00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:38.958
that I refuse to discuss

00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:40.625
because being vulnerable
scares me.

00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:41.875
I make dangerous choices

00:04:41.958 --> 00:04:43.291
because I have an unhealthy
bunny hero complex.

00:04:43.375 --> 00:04:45.916
And I didn't join the ZPD
because I wanted to be a cop.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.041
I joined because I always
wanted to be part of a pack.

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:51.416
And the thought of losing you
scares me because...

00:04:52.916 --> 00:04:54.125
because you're my pack.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.750
I should never have left you,

00:04:56.833 --> 00:04:58.833
and I do need
a herd of therapy animals.

00:04:58.916 --> 00:05:01.333
And I should have told you
that you are the only partner

00:05:01.416 --> 00:05:05.041
I would ever want because...
[sobs] ...you're my fluffle.

00:05:05.708 --> 00:05:07.000
Mmm. Um...

00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:08.833
[crying]
That's a bunch of rabbits.

00:05:08.916 --> 00:05:10.291
[both chuckle]

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:11.375
[Nibbles] Hmm.

00:05:11.458 --> 00:05:14.541
Now that is what we call
an overshare.

00:05:14.625 --> 00:05:16.666
I'm alive by the way.
I made it.

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.500
Oh! Also that guy
is still alive.

00:05:20.291 --> 00:05:22.083
[cackles]

00:05:22.166 --> 00:05:24.583
-[♪ upbeat music playing]
-Hey! Hey! Thief!

00:05:24.666 --> 00:05:26.750
He's gonna get to
the lost reptile neighborhood,

00:05:26.833 --> 00:05:29.166
find Gary's great-grandma's
patent and destroy it.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.500
Yeah, I've got no idea what
that means, or who Gary is,

00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:32.625
but let's go!

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.333
-Hopps and Wilde?
-Wilde and Hopps.

00:05:35.416 --> 00:05:37.375
And Nibbles and Gary!

00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:38.500
[gasps] He's Gary.

00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:40.291
Whoa, whoa!

00:05:40.833 --> 00:05:43.875
Thank you. It's for the snake.
He's cold. No fur on him.

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:45.375
-Why, you little...
-[chuckles] Bye now.

00:05:47.083 --> 00:05:48.208
[panting]

00:05:48.291 --> 00:05:49.875
-You!
-Dad!

00:05:49.958 --> 00:05:50.875
You don't belong
in this family!

00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:51.791
Wait, wait, wait! Dad!

00:05:51.875 --> 00:05:53.916
You will never
belong in this family!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.125
Wait, wait! I wasn't working
with them. I was helping us.

00:05:57.208 --> 00:05:58.916
[grunting]

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.500
I know where the reptile
neighborhood is buried.

00:06:01.583 --> 00:06:03.083
Where to find the real patent

00:06:03.166 --> 00:06:06.291
that proves that snakes
invented the walls.

00:06:06.375 --> 00:06:09.666
I'm going to destroy it,
for the family.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.708
For you, Daddy.

00:06:12.791 --> 00:06:15.125
[Winddancer blusters] Uh...

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:18.083
You want to keep your job,
you say nothing.

00:06:18.875 --> 00:06:19.958
You!

00:06:20.541 --> 00:06:22.708
Maybe you are a Lynxley.

00:06:22.791 --> 00:06:24.208
Take me to the patent.

00:06:24.291 --> 00:06:25.708
[rattling]

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.333
It takes a threesome
to be somethin',

00:06:29.416 --> 00:06:32.333
but a four-way
to bust your doorway.

00:06:33.541 --> 00:06:35.291
[Pawbert exclaims]

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:38.583
Get to the patent! Destroy it!

00:06:38.666 --> 00:06:40.375
[Pawbert grunting, panting]

00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:42.625
Go! We got this.

00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:46.833
Hey, whiskers,
you're done hurtin' muh city.

00:06:46.916 --> 00:06:48.125
[growling]

00:06:48.208 --> 00:06:49.708
Uh-oh. Tides have turned.

00:06:49.791 --> 00:06:50.875
-[Nibbles grunting]
-[lynxes roar and screech]

00:06:50.958 --> 00:06:52.458
[Nibbles]
Hey, Brian Winddancer!

00:06:52.541 --> 00:06:53.375
[thudding]

00:06:53.458 --> 00:06:57.250
You want to be a hero, or
just play one on TV? Ow!

00:06:57.333 --> 00:06:58.708
[♪ tense music playing]

00:07:00.333 --> 00:07:02.041
[panting]

